  "content": {
    "title": "TGL Finals highlights: LAGC wins 2 points on final hole, wins Match 1",
    "text": "Updated March 23, 2026, 11:30 p.m. ETTiger's team is now behind the 8 ball.Tiger Woods' Jupiter Links Golf Club led 5-4 heading to the final hole on Monday in the the 2026 TGL Finals, but Los Angeles Golf Club won the 15th hole, which was worth two points, to win Match 1 6-5 and take a 1-0 series lead.It's a best-of-three series and next up is Match 2 and the \"if necessary\" Match 3 on Tuesday.Get caught up right here will all the highlights and updates from Monday night. TGL Finals: Jupiter Links vs. Los Angeles leaderboardFinal: Los Angeles 6, Jupiter 5. LAGC wins final hole to win the matchAfter Kevin Kisner just missed a chip shot on the final hole, LAGC won the final hole, and the two points, to claim the match 6-5 and take a 1-0 match lead in the best-of-three finals.Jupiter will now have to win two matches on Tuesday to win the SoFi Cup. Stone & Steeple is the final hole, worth two pointsThere will be a winner after the 15th and final hole, one way or another. Down a point, LAGC can win the match 6-5 with a win on the 15th. Of course, Jupiter would win the match 7-4 with a win on this final hole. Max Homa drove the green and that would lead to a Jupiter pointHoma became the first to drive green on the hole dubbed \"Cut the Sails\", hitting it 336 yards to about 41 feet.Kevin Kisner wins a point on CenoteKisner hit the second-closest tee shot this season on the wild Cenote 11th hole on the TGL virtual course and L.A. would end up conceding the point, knottin things up once again.Justin Rose chips in from 35 feet for birdieDown 2-1, Los Angeles was still not on the green in two on the eighth hole but no matter, not when Justin Rose has wedge in hand, as he chipped in from 35 feet for a birdie and L.A.'s second point of the night. Charlie Woods is in attendance, wearing a Florida State hatRecent Florida State commit Charlie Woods (son of Tiger) was seen in the crowd sporting a Seminoles hat.A Tommy Fleetwood miss gives Jupiter a pointOn the sixth, Jupiter got another point after L.A. missed another short putt, this time it was Fleetwood who can't jar it.LAGC takes early lead, but would later give it upL.A. took an early lead 1-0 thanks to a point-clinching putt from Tommy Fleetwood on the second hole. On the sixth hole, Sahith Theegala missed a three-footer for bogey and that gave Jupiter a point to knot things up. How much money is up for grabs in the TGL?The winning team will split a $9 million first-place prize. That breaks down to $2.25 million per player. The second-place team will share $4.5 million, third gets $2.25 million, fourth is good for $2 million, fifth splits $1.75 million and last place shares $1.5 million. Who's playing in the 2026 TGL Finals?Tiger Woods, still sidelined after back surgery in October, will be in attendance once again for his Jupiter Links squad. He's fielding a team of Max Homa, Tom Kim and Kevin Kisner while LAGC counters with Tommy Fleetwood, Sahith Theegala and Justin Rose. Who is the TGL Chief Grass Officer?Yes, there is a such a thing. His name is Tanner Coffman. The course on Monday is playing 5,772 yards.Who's playing TGL this week who's also playing in Houston?Kim of Jupiter and Theegala of LA are both on the field list for this week's Texas Children's Houston Open on the PGA Tour, which starts Thursday.Who's the betting favorite for the 2026 TGL Finals?Fan Duel has LAGC as the favorite at -163, while Jupiter is +125 heading into Monday's Match 1.TGL Finals 2026 scheduleMatch 1: Jupiter Links GC vs. Los Angeles Golf ClubDate: Monday, March 23Time: 9 p.m. ETTV: ESPN2, ESPN appStream: Fubo, ESPN+Match 2: Los Angeles Golf Club vs. Jupiter Links GCDate: Tuesday, March 24Time: 7 p.m. ETTV: ESPNStream: Fubo, ESPN+Match 3: Los Angeles Golf Club vs. Jupiter Links GC (if necessary)Date: Tuesday, March 24Time: 9 p.m. ETTV: ESPNStream: Fubo, ESPN+",
